The optative is formed either with the suffix ''-eyyā-'' and the primary or secondary endings or with the suffix ''-e-'' and the secondary endings.<ref>Oberlies (2001: 223-224)</ref><ref>Perniola (1997: 85-86)</ref> They are added to the present stem, but the final vowel of the stem is dropped, so there is no difference between the conjugations. Besides wishes, the optative may express a possible or unreal action in conditional constructions.<ref>Perniola (1997: 354-356, 396-399)</ref>
